# keur secret/PII control — database dump or embedded data file committed.
#
# Why this exists: guide item #4 — db.sqlite3 / dump.sql get committed as "just
# test data" but often carry production rows or PII, and are unsuitable for git
# (large binaries, noisy diffs). Flag the well-known data-file shapes.
#
# WARN, not block: a data file is usually a mistake but occasionally intended
# (a fixture, a seed). WARN nudges a look without stopping every commit; genuine
# secrets inside are caught by the content secret rules regardless.
#
# @see the "never commit" guides (db.sqlite3, dump.sql, *.mdf).
id: KEUR-SECRET-011
maturity: 1
title: Database dump or data file committed
category: secret
severity: warning
engine: file-presence
action: warn
target:
  filenames: dump.sql db.sqlite3 database.sqlite
  extensions: .sqlite .sqlite3 .mdf
  exclude_paths: eval/corpus/repos/ tests/ test/ fixtures/ vendor/ build/ dist/
message: "A database dump / data file is committed — it may hold production data or PII and bloats the repo. Keep it out of git (seed from a script or fixture instead). @see KEUR-SECRET-011"
confidence: 0.7
fix: "Remove the data file from the repo (and history if it held real data), add the pattern to .gitignore, and seed test data from a small committed fixture or a script rather than a full dump."
